    "id": "blog-cjc-1295-no-dac-guide",
    "slug": "cjc-1295-no-dac-guide",
    "title": "CJC-1295 (No DAC): Molecular Profile & GHRH Pathway Analysis",
    "excerpt": "Examine the modified tetrasubstituted 29-amino acid GHRH analog CJC-1295 without DAC, its pulsatile release kinetics, and half-life differentiation.",
    "category": "Compound Spotlights",
    "tags": [
      "CJC-1295",
      "GHRH",
      "Mod GRF 1-29",
      "Endocrine Research",
      "Pulsatile Kinetics"
    ],
    "readTime": "10 min read",
    "author": "Dr. Marcus Vance, Ph.D.",
    "publishedAt": "2025-02-15",
    "image": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1579154204601-01588f351e67?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80",
    "content": "> **Research Takeaway:** CJC-1295 No DAC (Modified GRF 1-29) is a tetrasubstituted 29-amino acid analog of Growth Hormone Releasing Hormone. By eliminating the Drug Affinity Complex (DAC), it preserves short-acting (~30 min) physiological pulsatile GH release without inducing constant receptor saturation.\n\n## Executive Overview: The GHRH Axis & Molecular Engineering\n\nGrowth Hormone Releasing Hormone (GHRH) is the hypothalamic master regulator of somatotroph cell secretion in the anterior pituitary. Native GHRH 1-29 possesses an extremely brief circulating half-life in mammalian models (< 7 minutes) due to rapid enzymatic cleavage by **Dipeptidyl Peptidase IV (DPP-IV)**.\n\nTo circumvent enzymatic degradation while maintaining natural, episodic secretory dynamics, medicinal chemists developed **Modified GRF 1-29**, widely referenced in research as **CJC-1295 No DAC**.\n\n---\n\n## Molecular Structure & Tetrasubstitution\n\nCJC-1295 No DAC modifies native GHRH (1-29) at four strategic amino acid positions:\n* **Position 2:** D-Alanine substituted for L-Alanine (protects against DPP-IV enzymatic cleavage)\n* **Position 8:** Glutamine substituted for Asparagine (prevents deamidation)\n* **Position 15:** D-Alanine substituted for Glycine (enhances alpha-helical structural stability)\n* **Position 27:** Leucine substituted for Methionine (prevents oxidative degradation)\n\n![Peptra Bio CJC-1295 No DAC Research Vial](/images/products/cjc-1295-no-dac.jpg)\n\n---\n\n## CJC-1295 with DAC vs CJC-1295 No DAC\n\nThe presence of the **Drug Affinity Complex (DAC)** (Maleimidopropionic acid) completely alters pharmacokinetic behavior:\n\n| Molecular Parameter | CJC-1295 (No DAC / Mod GRF 1-29) | CJC-1295 (With DAC) |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Molecular Structure** | 29 Amino Acids (Tetrasubstituted) | 29 Amino Acids + Linker + Maleimido Acid |\n| **Albumin Binding Affinity** | Low (Free circulating peptide) | Very High (Covalent conjugation to serum albumin) |\n| **Biological Half-Life** | ~30 minutes | 6 to 8 days |\n| **Secretory Pattern** | Episodic / Pulsatile GH pulses | Continuous, basal elevated GH & IGF-1 |\n| **Receptor Desensitization Risk**| Low (Maintains physiological rhythm) | Moderate (Continuous somatotroph activation) |\n| **Synergy with GHRPs** | Outstanding (Additive pituitary pulse) | Blunted pulse discrimination |\n\n---\n\n## Preclinical Pharmacokinetics & Subcutaneous Dynamics\n\n![Laboratory Spectrometry & Peptide Analysis](https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1530497610245-94d3c16cda28?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1000&q=80)\n\nIn rodent and primate endocrine models, subcutaneous delivery of CJC-1295 No DAC exhibits consistent pharmacokinetic parameters:\n* **Time to Peak Plasma Concentration (Tmax):** 15 to 30 minutes post-administration.\n* **Duration of GH Pulse:** 90 to 120 minutes before plasma GH concentrations return to baseline.\n* **IGF-1 Modulation:** Repeated pulsatile administration results in a physiological 1.5x to 2.2x increase in serum IGF-1 without blunting endogenous pituitary response.\n\n### Somatostatin Interplay & Synergistic GHRP Co-Administration\nEndogenous somatostatin acts as a potent negative feedback inhibitor of GH release. In preclinical protocols:\n* CJC-1295 No DAC activates the **adenylyl cyclase / cAMP / Protein Kinase A (PKA)** pathway.\n* Co-administering a Ghrelin Receptor (GHSR-1a) agonist such as **Ipamorelin** activates the **Phospholipase C (PLC) / IP3 / Protein Kinase C (PKC)** pathway.\n* Simultaneous activation of both second-messenger cascades yields a synergistic GH surge significantly greater than the sum of either peptide alone.\n\n---\n\n## Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)\n\n### Why is CJC-1295 No DAC often referred to as Mod GRF 1-29?\nHistorically, \"CJC-1295\" was patented with the DAC (Drug Affinity Complex) technology. The compound synthesized without the DAC component is chemically identical to Modified GRF (1-29). The scientific literature uses Mod GRF 1-29 and CJC-1295 No DAC synonymously.\n\n### How does CJC-1295 No DAC resist DPP-IV enzymatic degradation?\nThe substitution of D-Alanine at position 2 alters the steric conformation of the peptide cleavage site, preventing Dipeptidyl Peptidase IV (DPP-IV) from cleaving the N-terminus.\n\n### What is the advantage of a short half-life in GH research?\nA ~30-minute half-life allows researchers to simulate natural mammalian pulsatile growth hormone secretion, avoiding the chronic hyper-stimulation and pituitary desensitization associated with long-acting secretagogues.\n\n### How should CJC-1295 No DAC be reconstituted and stored?\nReconstitute with bacteriostatic water (0.9% benzyl alcohol). Store lyophilized powder at -20°C and refrigerated liquid solutions at 2°C–8°C away from light.\n\n### Is CJC-1295 approved for clinical human treatment?\nNo. CJC-1295 No DAC is strictly an investigational research chemical intended for in vitro assays and laboratory animal models.\n\n---\n\n## Research Use Only Disclaimer\n\nThis document is compiled solely for scientific education and preclinical research reference. Peptra Bio compounds are strictly designated for laboratory research use only.\n\n---\n\n## Key References\n\n1. Teichman SL, et al. *Prolonged stimulation of growth hormone (GH) and insulin-like growth factor I secretion by CJC-1295.* J Clin Endocrinol Metab. 2006;91(3):799-805.\n2. Ionescu M, Frohman LA. *Pulsatile secretion of growth hormone (GH) persists during continuous stimulation by CJC-1295.* J Clin Endocrinol Metab. 2006;91(12):4792-4797.\n3. Alba M, et al. *Once-daily administration of CJC-1295 normalizes growth in the GHRH knockout mouse.* Am J Physiol Endocrinol Metab. 2006;291(6):E1290-E1294."
