    "image": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1584308666744-24d5c474f2ae?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80",
    "content": "> **Research Takeaway:** Ipamorelin is recognized as the most selective synthetic Growth Hormone Secretagogue Receptor (GHSR-1a) agonist. Unlike earlier generation GHRPs, it stimulates robust Growth Hormone secretion without inducing off-target surges in Cortisol, Prolactin, or ACTH.\n\n## Executive Overview: Pentapeptide Selectivity & Pharmacology\n\n**Ipamorelin** (Aib-His-D-2-Nal-D-Phe-Lys-NH2) is a synthetic pentapeptide developed as a third-generation growth hormone secretagogue (GHS). It mimics the biological activity of ghrelin by binding directly to the **growth hormone secretagogue receptor 1a (GHSR-1a)** in the anterior pituitary gland.\n\nEarlier secretagogues (such as GHRP-6 and GHRP-2) frequently triggered secondary elevations in plasma cortisol and prolactin levels. Ipamorelin was specifically engineered to eliminate these off-target endocrine disruptions.\n\n---\n\n## Chemical Profile & Receptor Dynamics\n\n* **Molecular Formula:** C38H49N9O5\n* **Molecular Weight:** 711.86 g/mol\n* **Sequence:** Aib-His-D-2-Nal-D-Phe-Lys-NH2\n* **Receptor Affinity:** Highly selective for pituitary GHSR-1a; negligible affinity for opioid or central adrenergic receptors.\n\n![Peptra Bio Ipamorelin 5mg Research Vial](/images/products/ipamorelin.jpg)\n\n### Intracellular Signaling Cascade\nBinding of Ipamorelin to GHSR-1a initiates a downstream G-protein coupled cascade:\n1. **PLC Activation:** Phospholipase C is activated, cleaving PIP2 into **IP3** (Inositol triphosphate) and **DAG** (Diacylglycerol).\n2. **Calcium Mobilization:** IP3 binds to endoplasmic reticulum receptors, causing a rapid transient influx of intracellular Ca²⁺.\n3. **Pulsatile Exocytosis:** Elevated calcium promotes the exocytosis of pre-stored Growth Hormone granules into the extracellular space.\n\n---\n\n## Comparative GHRP Selectivity Matrix\n\n| Secretagogue Compound | GH Release Potency | Cortisol Stimulation | Prolactin Elevation | Appetite Stimulation (NPY) |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Ipamorelin** | High | Undetectable / Baseline | Undetectable / Baseline | Minimal |\n| **GHRP-6** | High | Mild to Moderate | Mild to Moderate | Very High (Potent hunger trigger) |\n| **GHRP-2 (Pralmorelin)** | Very High | Significant Elevation | Significant Elevation | Moderate |\n| **Hexarelin** | Extremely High | High Elevation | High Elevation | Low (Rapid desensitization) |\n\n---\n\n## Preclinical Research Applications\n\n![Endocrine Laboratory Investigation](https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1579154204601-01588f351e67?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1000&q=80)\n\n### 1. Bone Mineral Density & Osteoblast Proliferation\nIn rodent models of osteopenia, longitudinal administration of Ipamorelin demonstrated significant increases in bone mineral content and femoral trabecular volume without altering systemic bone remodeling markers abnormally.\n\n### 2. Gastrointestinal Motility Assays\nBecause GHSR-1a receptors are expressed across the enteric nervous system, Ipamorelin has been studied in postoperative ileus models, showing accelerated gastric emptying and restoration of bowel motility.\n\n### 3. Nitrogen Balance & Lean Mass Preservation\nIn catabolic animal models, Ipamorelin supported positive nitrogen retention and attenuated glucocorticoid-induced muscle wasting.\n\n---\n\n## Reconstitution, Storage & Handling Standards\n\n* **Solvent:** Bacteriostatic Water (0.9% Benzyl Alcohol) is recommended for standard multi-entry research assays.\n* **Storage (Lyophilized):** Stable at -20°C for up to 24 months.\n* **Storage (Reconstituted):** Maintain between 2°C and 8°C. Solutions should be utilized within 28 days of reconstitution.\n\n---\n\n## Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)\n\n### What makes Ipamorelin different from GHRP-6 and GHRP-2?\nIpamorelin is far more selective. While GHRP-6 and GHRP-2 stimulate cortisol, ACTH, and prolactin alongside growth hormone, Ipamorelin triggers pure GH release without elevating stress hormones.\n\n### Does Ipamorelin cause desensitization of the pituitary receptor?\nUnlike Hexarelin, which causes rapid tachyphylaxis (receptor down-regulation), Ipamorelin exhibits minimal desensitization during repeated administration cycles in preclinical studies.\n\n### Why is Ipamorelin frequently studied in combination with CJC-1295?\nIpamorelin (a GHRP) and CJC-1295 (a GHRH analog) stimulate GH release through distinct intracellular pathways (PLC/Ca²⁺ vs cAMP/PKA). When administered together, they produce a synergistic GH pulse.\n\n### What is the typical shelf life of reconstituted Ipamorelin 5mg?\nStored at 2°C–8°C in bacteriostatic water, Ipamorelin remains stable with >95% purity for up to 28 days.\n\n### Is Ipamorelin approved for human clinical use?\nNo. Ipamorelin is an investigational peptide strictly manufactured for in vitro biochemical and animal research use.\n\n---\n\n## Research Use Only Disclaimer\n\nThis guide is provided for educational and scientific research purposes only. Peptra Bio supplies peptides strictly for laboratory in vitro experimentation.\n\n---\n\n## Key References\n\n1. Raun K, et al. *Ipamorelin, the first selective growth hormone secretagogue.* Eur J Endocrinol. 1998;139(5):552-561.\n2. Gobburu JV, et al. *Pharmacokinetic-pharmacodynamic modeling of ipamorelin-stimulated growth hormone release in rodents.* Pharm Res. 1999;16(9):1412-1416.\n3. Svensson J, et al. *The GH secretagogues ipamorelin and GHRP-6 increase bone mineral content in adult female rats.* J Endocrinol. 2000;165(3):569-577."
