    "title": "Selank Heptapeptide: Molecular Structure & Receptor Modulation Guide",
    "excerpt": "Examine the regulatory heptapeptide Selank, its tuftsin-derived sequence, allosteric GABA-A modulation, and preclinical neuroprotective properties.",
    "category": "Compound Spotlights",
    "tags": [
      "Selank",
      "Neuropeptides",
      "GABA",
      "BDNF",
      "Nootropic Research"
    ],
    "readTime": "9 min read",
    "author": "Dr. Marcus Vance, Ph.D.",
    "publishedAt": "2025-02-15",
    "image": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1579154204601-01588f351e67?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80",
    "content": "> **Research Takeaway:** Selank is a synthetic heptapeptide derived from the endogenous immunomodulatory peptide Tuftsin. In neurobiological research, it acts as an allosteric modulator of GABA-A receptors, elevates BDNF expression, and inhibits enkephalin-degrading enzymes.\n\n## Executive Overview: Heptapeptide Neurobiology\n\n**Selank** (Thr-Lys-Pro-Arg-Pro-Gly-Pro) was developed at the Institute of Molecular Genetics of the Russian Academy of Sciences. It combines the naturally occurring tetrapeptide **Tuftsin** (Thr-Lys-Pro-Arg)—a peptide produced by spleen tissue—with a C-terminal Pro-Gly-Pro tripeptide sequence designed to confer metabolic stability.\n\nIn preclinical central nervous system (CNS) models, Selank exhibits anxiolytic, cognitive-enhancing, and immunomodulatory properties without the sedative, addictive, or myorelaxant side-effects typical of classic benzodiazepines.\n\n---\n\n## Chemical Profile & Sequence Architecture\n\n* **Sequence:** Thr-Lys-Pro-Arg-Pro-Gly-Pro (TKPRPGP)\n* **Molecular Formula:** C33H57N11O9\n* **Molecular Weight:** 751.87 g/mol\n* **Structural Engineering:** The addition of the Pro-Gly-Pro fragment prevents rapid carboxy-peptidase breakdown, extending central nervous system bioavailability.\n\n![Peptra Bio Selank Research Vial](/images/products/selank.jpg)\n\n---\n\n## Neuro-Chemical Mechanisms of Action\n\n### 1. GABA-A Receptor Allosteric Modulation\nSelank does not bind directly to the benzodiazepine site; rather, it allosterically modulates GABA-A receptor affinity, enhancing endogenous GABAergic inhibitory transmission during acute stress.\n\n### 2. Neurotrophin Expression (BDNF & NGF)\nIn rodent hippocampal tissue studies, administration of Selank induced significant upregulation of **Brain-Derived Neurotrophic Factor (BDNF)** and its high-affinity receptor TrkB, supporting synaptic plasticity and memory formation.\n\n### 3. Enkephalin Degradation Inhibition\nSelank competitively inhibits serum and tissue **enkephalinases** (aminopeptidases and carboxypeptidases), extending the half-life of endogenous opioid peptides (enkephalins) and supporting neuroprotective stability.\n\n---\n\n## Comparative Matrix: Selank vs Semax\n\n| Characteristic | Selank (TKPRPGP) | Semax (MEHFPGP) |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Origin Peptide** | Derived from Tuftsin (Immune origin) | Derived from ACTH (4-10) (Adrenocortical origin) |\n| **Primary Research Profile**| Anxiolytic, stress-resilience, GABAergic | Nootropic, psychostimulant, dopaminergic |\n| **Neurotransmitter Modulation**| GABA, Serotonin (5-HT), Enkephalins | Dopamine, Serotonin, Acetylcholine |\n| **BDNF Upregulation** | Moderate to High in Hippocampus | Very High across Frontal Cortex & Hippocampus |\n| **Motor Activity Effect** | Calming / Normalizing | Stimulatory / Vigilance promoting |\n\n---\n\n## Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)\n\n### What is the relationship between Selank and Tuftsin?\nSelank is an elongated analog of the human tetrapeptide Tuftsin (TKPR). The addition of the Pro-Gly-Pro tripeptide protects the compound from enzymatic degradation while preserving its biological signaling.\n\n### Does Selank create dependency or sedation in animal models?\nNo. Preclinical rodent studies demonstrate that Selank acts via allosteric modulation rather than direct benzodiazepine receptor occupancy, producing no signs of physical dependence, sedation, or withdrawal.\n\n### How does Selank affect BDNF levels in the brain?\nIn in vitro and animal assays, Selank significantly upregulates hippocampal BDNF mRNA expression, which is associated with enhanced neuronal survival and long-term potentiation.\n\n### What are the proper storage guidelines for Selank?\nStore dry lyophilized vials at -20°C. Once reconstituted with bacteriostatic water, refrigerate at 2°C–8°C away from light and use within 28 days.\n\n### Is Selank approved for human medical prescription worldwide?\nSelank is approved as an anxiolytic in Russia and certain CIS nations, but remains an investigational research compound in the United States, EU, and UK.\n\n---\n\n## Research Use Only Disclaimer\n\nThis profile is designed exclusively for scientific education and preclinical research reference. Peptra Bio supplies peptides strictly for laboratory in vitro investigation.\n\n---\n\n## Key References\n\n1. Kozlovskaia MM, et al. *Studies of the anxiolytic action of the peptide drug Selank.* Zh Nevrol Psikhiatr Im S S Korsakova. 2003;103(11):37-41.\n2. Semenova TP, et al. *Comparison of the effects of Selank and classic tranquilizers on learning and memory.* Bull Exp Biol Med. 2010;149(2):161-164.\n3. Kost NV, et al. *Enkephalinase-inhibiting properties of the heptapeptide Selank.* Bioorg Khim. 2001;27(6):448-451."
